Dependency removed (1NF -> 2NF): Removed partial dependencies on parts of the composite key by separating attributes that depend only on customer_ref, only on meter_code, or only on battery_bank_code into their own entities.

Second Normal Form (2NF)

Attributes depending only on a single entity key are separated from time-specific reading attributes:

Meters / Customers slice:
| meter_code | customer_ref | battery_bank_code | tariff_rate | credit_balance |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| M-10 | C-01 | BB-1 | 0.20 | 14.34 |
| M-11 | C-02 | BB-1 | 0.20 | 0.50 |
| M-12 | C-03 | BB-2 | 0.22 | 8.00 |

Consumption logs slice (meter_code, reading_time):
| meter_code | reading_time | kwh_used |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| M-10 | 2026-03-04 08:00 | 1.2 |
| M-10 | 2026-03-04 09:00 | 0.8 |
| M-11 | 2026-03-04 08:00 | 2.5 |

Dependency removed (2NF -> 3NF): Removed transitive dependencies where non-key attributes depended on another non-key attribute (for example, zone_name belongs to the customer/service area rather than the meter reading, and battery telemetry belongs to the battery_bank_code timeline rather than individual customer meters).

Third Normal Form (3NF)

Every non-key attribute depends solely on the primary key of its own table:

CUSTOMERS: (customer_id [PK], zone_name, account_status)

BATTERY_BANKS: (battery_bank_id [PK], nominal_voltage, rated_capacity_ah, zone_name)

METERS: (meter_id [PK], customer_id [FK], battery_bank_id [FK], meter_status, tariff_rate, credit_balance)

CONSUMPTION_LOGS: (consumption_id [PK], meter_id [FK], reading_timestamp, kwh_consumed)

BATTERY_HEALTH_LOGS: (health_log_id [PK], battery_bank_id [FK], recorded_at, voltage_v, current_a, temp_c, soc_pct, soh_pct)

MAINTENANCE_ALERTS: (alert_id [PK], meter_id [FK, nullable], battery_bank_id [FK, nullable], alert_type, severity, status, created_at)

